Changes: strict CP949 decoding of the CSV files; active-status meal facilities and shelters in use only, every protection-zone facility category; bare native single-lot address extraction; meal-register EPSG:5174 to longitude/latitude EPSG:4326 conversion with PROJ, the other registers' own EPSG:4326 longitude/latitude unchanged; duplicate removal; shared-point and coordinate-spread quarantine across all three registers; an address the meal register supplies keeps its meal-register points. The builder admits only geometry-corroborated lots whose folded name/number pair was absent from its earlier Korean inputs. Every institution or facility category is eligible. No benchmark or held-out answers select source rows.

These are registered facility parcel/address reference points, not verified entrances or complete residential coverage. Protection-zone points locate the target facility, not the zone. Lot-derived houses are excluded from house reverse-geocoding postings. Multi-parcel, floor/unit annotations and ambiguous or unsupported source records are not admitted by this supplement. Existing house coordinates and postcodes take precedence.
